  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Finely chop or crush garlic.\n• In a medium saucepan, melt half the butter with a dash of olive oil over medium heat.\n• Cook garlic until fragrant, 1-2 mins. Add basmati rice, the water (for the rice) and a generous pinch of salt, then bring to the boil.\n• Reduce heat to low and cover with a lid. Cook for 10 mins, then remove from heat and keep covered until rice is tender and water is absorbed, 10 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6a4cc569fc37702f5b7aea4a/step-15852a00.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, roughly chop cucumber, tomato and red onion.\n• Drain and rinse chickpeas.\n• In a medium bowl, combine the white wine vinegar and a good pinch of sugar and salt.\n• Scrunch half the onion, then add to pickling liquid with just enough water to cover.Set aside.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6a4cc569fc37702f5b7aea4a/step-171fab10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a large frying pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat.\n• Cook chickpeas and remaining onion, tossing, until softened, 4-5 mins.\n• Add tomato paste and chermoula spice blend and cook until fragrant 1 min.\n• Stir in coconut milk, the salt, water (for the chickpeas) and remaining butter and simmer until slightly thickened, 2-3 mins. Season to taste.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6a4cc569fc37702f5b7aea4a/step-26c5cf20.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Drain pickled onion. Add cucumber, tomato and a drizzle of olive oil to the drained onion. Season to taste.\n• Divide garlic rice and Persian-spiced coconut chickpeas between bowls. Top with zingy chopped salad to serve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6a4cc569fc37702f5b7aea4a/step-b6519530.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
